A||||8||stsmithgt||Leaking exhaust manifold||||8
Z||000000||stsmithgt||11-26-1999||07:38 PM||||I've got a mechanic soon to be my former mechanic.<BR>After my third visit to get him to stop a leak from <BR>my exhaust manifold, he tells me about a piece of sheetmetal in between the<BR>manifold and the head besides the gasket(one), he put in.<BR>This should have raised a flag in his head.  I was<BR>hoping to confirm information I've come up with that<BR>that sheetmetal is actually an old factory gasket.<BR>I hope somewone has some info. on it so I can spoon<BR>feed this mechanic through this warranty work so I can<BR>terminate my contact with him.  Besides who in there right <BR>mind only seals up one side of a spacer or sheetmetal<BR>on a manifold, unless the sheetmetal has it's own crush<BR>rings around the ports.  He only used one new gasket on the manifold <BR>with that piece of metal in between the manifold, not that two <BR>would have corrected the problem. Thanks for the read<BR>while I let off steam.  86 gt 4spd. 2.8 <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif">||||reg||8
Z||000001||Bruce||11-26-1999||08:38 PM||||Did you try to get the manifold fixed through the factory recall program?||||reg||5
Z||000002||WKDFIRO||11-27-1999||04:15 AM||||On the back manifolds is a heat shield to keep heat away from the AC pump. The shield is attached to 3 studs on the manifold. The shield is not supposed to be the gasket or even put on with the gasket. There are 3 bolts for the manifold and 3 studs to bolt down the manifold and have the heat shield bolted on top of that. You might check to find out if someone bright tried to use the shield as a gasket. <P>I also seem to remember that the recall on some V6s put this additional shield that may have gone under the gasket. It was a complete overkill based on the 84 fires. Ive seen only a few with this sheild intact. The shield looked like it would protect from oil leaking from the valve covers. What it was protecting was always the question. The sheet metal in question was a bungled recall. So few Fieros have it with the rest not having any probs your mechanic can probably just toss it or you can keep it for your own piece of mind. If I saw a picture of this sheet metal I would be more positive.<p>[This message has been edited by WKDFIRO (edited 11-27-1999).]||||reg||1
Z||000003||TOM||11-27-1999||11:26 AM||||It was designed to keep leaking oil from driping on the catalytic convertor. Since these run so hot it could ignite the oil||||reg||1
Z||000004||stsmithgt||11-27-1999||11:32 AM||||Yeah!  I'll toss the thing.  I couldn't find a<BR>picture of it, but maybe I can get the old one and<BR>make one at work. we do it with circuit boards so<BR>I hope they don't mind a crusty board looking thing.<BR>As for the other heatshield, I do have that one on.  I<BR>made sure he didn't toss that one.  I'm not saying this <BR>michanic is stupid, he just needs more information.  The <BR>way they kept trying to pass me my car still with an<BR>exhaust leak is why I'm dumping this place.  They must<BR>have thought I was deaf.(Wayside Automotive in Sand City California)<BR>Thanks again for your comments. S. Todd Smith, Marina CA.<BR>||||reg||10
Z||000005||theogre||11-27-1999||11:49 AM||||I'm reading this right....... They took off heat shields and discarded them. Making the car less safe to drive.<P>It it thier reposnsibility to obtain replacements. If they refuse to do so, the get replacements, preferably from a GM dealer, have them installed, and then sue the idiots in small claims court for the enitre costs, including court fees if your state allows that. Some allow adding court fees to demands other don't.<P>You should also file a BBB complaint.||||reg||1
Z||000006||stsmithgt||11-29-1999||09:51 AM||||I still have the two heat shields.  It's just the mechanic can't get the one between the manifold and the head to stop leaking.  I don't know if the shield had it's own crush rings to seal it or if one gasket on each side is the way to solve the problem.  It's obvious to me the mechanic needs some spoon feeding to get through this situation.  I'm about ready to toss that shield and just get a bigger fire exstinguisher for my car.  I don't have oil leaks at this time anyway.  After a weekend of cooling down, I hope they are ready for a civilized conversation and a conclusion to this matter.  I've got other projects to do to my car that have had to be put on the back burner longer than desired.  <BR>Happy Holidays everyone anyways. <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif">||||reg||1
